Clarifying how to present the requested sections.

Clarifying how to present the requested sections.

Done

Got it. From here on, I'll give you the code for each step in sections, with an explanation of each section, and you assemble and test.

Step 7b: The gallery grid

This assumes you've already created src/utils.ts and src/pages/GalleryView.module.css from my last message. If not, do those first.

Section 1: Imports and props (top of GalleryView.tsx)

import { Link } from 'react-router';
import type { ApodPicture } from '../types';
import { getImageUrl } from '../utils';
import styles from './GalleryView.module.css';

interface GalleryViewProps {
  pictures: ApodPicture[];
}

This is the same pattern as ListView: the router's Link, the shared type, the image helper, and the CSS Module. styles is an object whose properties are your CSS class names (styles.grid, styles.image).

Section 2: The component logic (Zone 2)

export default function GalleryView({ pictures }: GalleryViewProps) {
  const withImages = pictures.filter((picture) => getImageUrl(picture) !== undefined);

This drops any entry that has no image to show, like a video with no thumbnail. !== means "is not exactly equal to."

Section 3: The JSX (Zone 3)

return (
    <div className={styles.grid}>
      {withImages.map((picture) => (
        <Link key={picture.date} to={`/apod/${picture.date}`}>
          <img className={styles.image} src={getImageUrl(picture)} alt={picture.title} />
        </Link>
      ))}
    </div>
  );
}

Here's how this fits together:

The outer <div> gets the grid class, so its children, the links, become grid tiles.

key goes on the Link because it's the outermost element returned by each .map() iteration. React needs the key on whatever sits directly in the list.

Each image is wrapped in a Link, so clicking it goes to the detail page. That's 10 rubric points.

Section 4: Pass the data in (App.tsx)

Change the gallery route to:

<Route path="/gallery" element={<GalleryView pictures={pictures} />} />

Test

The Gallery page shows a grid of square images.

Resizing the browser window changes the number of columns.

Clicking an image goes to /mp2/apod/<that date>.

When those work, commit and push, and tell me. Next is Step 7d: the gallery filter. We'll filter by month, with a button for each month that you can toggle on and off, so users can select one or several at once.

