Tracking down a missing stylesheet file.

Tracking down a missing stylesheet file.

Done

That error means Vite can't find GalleryView.module.css. The ^ arrow points at the import, and the file either doesn't exist or isn't where the import says it is.

The ./ in './GalleryView.module.css' means "in the same folder as this file." Since GalleryView.tsx is in src/pages/, Vite is looking for src/pages/GalleryView.module.css.

Step 1: See what's actually in the folder

In your second terminal (inside mp2), run:

ls src src/pages

This lists both folders. Compare what you see against what should be there:

src:
  App.tsx  main.tsx  types.ts  utils.ts  api  pages  ...

src/pages:
  DetailView.tsx  GalleryView.tsx  GalleryView.module.css  ListView.tsx

Step 2: Fix whichever of these you find

The CSS file isn't in src/pages. It may have been saved in src/ or the project root. Move it into src/pages/.

The name is slightly off, for example GalleryView.css (missing .module), galleryView.module.css (wrong capitalization), or GalleryView.module.css.txt (TextEdit on Mac sometimes adds .txt). Rename it to exactly GalleryView.module.css.

The file doesn't exist at all. Create it in src/pages/ from your editor, and paste in the CSS from Step 7c:

.grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(200px, 1fr));
  gap: 12px;
}

.image {
  width: 100%;
  aspect-ratio: 1;
  object-fit: cover;
  display: block;
